Imported: README.md, LICENSE, src/, demo/, test/src/, and the upstream
selftest, demotest, misctest, logform and chartest scripts. Browser and
macOS front ends are not included.

The incomplete beta routine in src/eval_incbeta.c is by Lewis Van Winkle,
copyright 2016, 2017, under the zlib license reproduced in that file.
It was already included in the pinned Eigenmath revision.

Local changes to Eigenmath:
  - src/defs.h selects the native Plan 9 declarations with PLAN9.
  - src/prototypes.h declares a void main for Plan 9.
  - src/eval_incbeta.c uses INFINITY rather than constant division by zero,
    which the Plan 9 compiler rejects. The numerical method is unchanged.
  - mkfile builds the core without upstream main.c and readfile.c, using
    plan9.c for console, file, pipe and error handling instead.

math/ imports double-precision routines from musl 1.2.5:
  Source: https://musl.libc.org/releases/musl-1.2.5.tar.gz
  SHA-256: a9a118bbe84d8764da0ea0d28b3ab3fae8477fc7e4085d90102b8596fc7c75e4
  License: math/COPYRIGHT, including MIT and the per-file Sun notices.

The sin, cos, tan, __tan, __rem_pio2 and __rem_pio2_large files reuse the
musl adaptations in generated9's QuickJS port at commit
4dc00e5a1463f87ca823923d916e1f5919cd09b7.
The remaining imported routines come directly from the archive above.

Math adaptations: exact hexadecimal floating constants are written in
decimal; double-only branches replace preprocessor expressions unsupported
by the native compiler; unused disabled code and the lgamma_r weak alias
are omitted; constant division by zero uses NaN/Inf; explicit sign-bit
negation preserves signed zero. libm.h supplies the needed native types
and bit operations. support.c supplies lgamma, sign-bit negation and the
zero/infinity cases missing from Plan 9 log. The upstream algorithms and
coefficient tables are preserved. The system libraries are unchanged.

New generated9 files use the repository's root LICENSE. Original authors'
notices must accompany source and binary redistribution.
